# Derived, and large. Everything here is reproducible from the two sibling repos
# by `./run prep`, so none of it belongs in the history.
cache/
runs/
out/

# figures/ IS tracked. It was previously ignored with an explicit per-file
# allow-list, and that broke twice: a figure added to the README after the list was
# written (paired_deltas.png, then model_comparison.png and three_way_comparison.png)
# renders as a broken image on GitHub, and nothing catches it. The whole top level
# is small -- well under 10 MB -- so tracking it wholesale removes the failure mode.
# Only the regenerable panel dump below is excluded.

# The databar panels are evidence for the scale recovery, but 51 of them is
# clutter. Keep the one frame the README quotes numbers from, so that claim stays
# checkable, and regenerate the rest with `./run scale`.
figures/databars/*
!figures/databars/260622_316_H_b2_front_CBS_01_databar.png

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store
